Ms. Achterberg,<br />
<br />
Marchwood completed its acquisition of the advisory book of Hollis Grange A=
dvisers, Inc. on September 30, 2013. Sixty-one client accounts transferred =
to us. Nobody has asked us for this and there is no examination open, but t=
he undertaking Marchwood gave the staff on June 2, 2011 is not limited in t=
ime and by its terms reaches accounts we acquire, so I am reporting what we=
 did with them.<br />
<br />
All 61 Hollis Grange accounts are now held at Signal Peak Trust Company und=
er the same custodial agreements as the rest of the book; the 53 that were =
not already there were transferred on October 14, 2013. Fourteen of them ar=
rived with a fee-debit authorization in favor of the prior adviser. Those a=
uthorizations were revoked rather than assigned to Marchwood, and the clien=
ts were re-papered onto Marchwood's standard agreement, which does not incl=
ude withdrawal authority.<br />
<br />
We have engaged Quillen and Marsh LLP to perform the surprise examination c=
overing calendar year 2013, on the assumption that the transition period is=
 one in which we could be deemed to have had custody. Form ADV-E will be fi=
led within 120 days of the examination date. A memorandum of the account tr=
ansfers and the revoked authorizations is attached for your file.<br />
<br />
Marguerite Vasseur-Kyle<br />
Chief Compliance Officer<br />
Marchwood Asset Management LLC
